  "losses_and_limits": [
    "Read-only by construction: a shared view refuses create/write/truncate/xattr/symlink/rename/link with EROFS. Writes remain on the single-mount path.",
    "One backend mutex per store serialises physical I/O across views; independent daemons overlap that I/O. Under concurrent large reads the shared server can be slower.",
    "A shared server pins views at open: there is no live re-read of commits made by another process while it runs (the same as any read-only mount).",
    "One process is a single failure domain: a panic in one view would end every view. The view callbacks are covered by tests and the shared read path uses no panics, but this is a real difference from independent daemons.",
    "Per-mount latency in shared mode includes sequential resolution and mounting of all views before the last one appears; compare `all_mounted_ms`, not only p50.",
    "No fleet or multi-host claim; one host, synthetic deterministic corpus, warm page cache."
